hadiths[7]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27965","Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq, from Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon me one day and said: Is there food. I said: No, except a bone given to a freedwoman of ours from charity. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then bring it near, for it has reached its lawful place."
"27966","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, the freedman of the family of Talhah, he said: I heard Kurayb narrating, from Ibn Abbas, from Juwayriyah, she said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed by Juwayriyah early in the morning while she was in the mosque supplicating, then he passed by her near midday, and said: You are still upon your state. She said: Yes. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not teach you words with which you may equal them; were they weighed with them, they would outweigh: Glory be to Allah, the number of His creation, Glory be to Allah, the number of His creation, three times; Glory be to Allah, the pleasure of Himself, Glory be to Allah, the pleasure of Himself, Glory be to Allah, the pleasure of Himself; Glory be to Allah, the weight of His Throne, Glory be to Allah, the weight of His Throne, Glory be to Allah, the weight of His Throne; Glory be to Allah, the ink of His words, Glory be to Allah, the ink of His words, Glory be to Allah, the ink of His words."
"27967","And her name was Barrah, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, named her Juwayriyah."
"27968","Muhammad and Hajjaj said: Shubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Ayyub, from Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her on a Friday while she was fasting, and said to her: Did you fast yesterday. She said: No. He said: Do you intend to fast tomorrow. She said: No. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Then break fast."
"27969","Aswad, meaning Ibn Amir, narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from his maternal aunt Umm Uthman, from al-Tufayl, the nephew of Juwayriyah, from Juwayriyah, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Whoever wears a garment of silk in this world, Allah, Exalted is He, shall clothe him a garment of disgrace, or a garment of fire."
"27970","Asim narrated to us: Layth ibn Sad narrated to us: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, he said: Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq claims that Juwayriyah, the wife of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, informed him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her and said: Is there food. She said: No, by Allah, we have no food except a bone of a sheep given to my freedwoman from charity. He, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Bring it near, for it has reached its lawful place."
"27971","Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: Abu Ayyub al-Ataki narrated to me, from Juwayriyah bint al-Harith, she said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entered upon her on a Friday while she was fasting, and said to her: Did you fast yesterday. She said: No. He said: Do you intend to fast tomorrow. She said: No. He said: Then break fast."
